.TH CURRENT_RELEASE.YAML 5 "2026-10-06" "mu2edaq-shifter-tools 1.1.0" "Mu2e DAQ Manual"
.SH NAME
current_release.yaml \- DAQ release description for daq-install-tools
.SH SYNOPSIS
.I config/current_release.yaml
.SH DESCRIPTION
Read by
.BR daq-install-tools (1),
which renders the two version strings, checks that the release paths
exist, and reports or creates the install directories. The file is
gitignored; copy \fIcurrent_release.example.yaml\fR to create it.
.SS Keys
.TP
.BR base_release ", " test_release
Mappings with \fBprefix\fR (string, default \fBd\fR), \fBmajor\fR,
\fBminor\fR, \fBpatch\fR (integers, zero-padded to two digits),
\fBsuffix\fR (optional) and \fBpath\fR. Rendered as
\fI<prefix><major>_<minor>_<patch>[_<suffix>]\fR, e.g.
\fBd09_00_00_alpha\fR. A missing or non-existent \fBpath\fR is an error
unless \fB\-\-override\fR is given.
.TP
.B install_path
Mapping with a required \fBbasepath\fR; every other key is a directory
joined onto it (e.g. \fBbin: bin\fR means \fI<basepath>/bin\fR).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I config/current_release.example.yaml
Shipped example.
.SH EXAMPLES
.RS
.nf
base_release: {prefix: d, major: 9, minor: 0, patch: 0,
               path: /mu2e/releases/v9_00_00}
test_release: {prefix: d, major: 9, minor: 0, patch: 0,
               suffix: alpha, path: /home/mu2edaq/test_rel_v9_00_00}
install_path: {basepath: /home/mu2edaq/daq\-tools, bin: bin, man: man}
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR daq-install-tools (1),
.BR daq-operations.yaml (5)
